A wrapper can add markup around each direct child. A list gives each child
its own list-item tags.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    list #= [$before "<li>", $after "</li>":<ul>[$slot]</ul>]
    steps = [list:[:Build][:Test]]
]

The outer body contributes the `<ul>` element. The two separate children
produce `<li>Build</li>` and `<li>Test</li>` inside it. A single child
containing both words would give you one list item.

You can use either directive on its own. Put `$fresh` on one child to skip
its immediate parent's prefix and suffix. For an example and the rules for
empty children and loops, see @../template-directives/#child-wrapping
(Wrapping direct children).
